        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "     1→# Release history\n     2→\n     3→### main branch\n     4→\n     5→- Expanded `ANTHROPIC_MODELS` list with Claude Opus 4.1/4.5/4.6/4.7 dated variants and Claude Sonnet 3.7 so the Anthropic API key auto-detection (`models.sanity_check_models`) recognises them.\n     6→- Added support for Claude 4.5/4.6 models and updated model aliases (sonnet/haiku/opus).\n     7→- Expanded Gemini model support with 2.5 Flash and Flash‑Lite, added Gemini 3 preview models, and updated the flash alias to gemini/gemini-flash-latest.\n     8→- Added DeepSeek Reasoner model and updated DeepSeek model metadata with costs and prompt caching.\n     9→- Added BadGatewayError and ImageFetchError to handled exceptions.\n    10→- Fixed exception mapping to only include real exception classes, avoiding runtime errors, by Claudia Pellegrino.\n    11→- Repo map now tags Fortran, Haskell, Julia, and Zig and is compatible with newer tree-sitter Python APIs, by Varchas Gopalaswamy, Tim Put, and Mubashir Osmani.\n    12→- Removed deprecated google-generativeai dependency to eliminate import warnings, by Mark McDonald.\n    13→- Added settings for new OpenAI GPT‑5.1/5.2 and GPT‑5‑pro models across OpenAI, Azure, and OpenRouter, including chat and codex variants.\n    14→- Changed the gemini alias to point to gemini/gemini-3-pro-preview.\n    15→- Added support for OpenAI o1-pro model.\n    16→- Added support for GPT‑5.3/5.4 model variants across OpenAI, Azure, and OpenRouter, plus GPT‑4.1‑nano.\n    17→- Added `/ok` as a shortcut for asking aider to go ahead with the proposed changes, with optional extra instructions.\n    18→- When auto-commits are disabled, aider can add files outside the git repo and promote read-only files to editable, by Chris McCormick.\n    19→- Fixed crashes caused by circular symlink loops when resolving paths, by coder_3.\n    20→- Aider wrote 62% of the code in this release.\n    21→\n    22→### Aider v0.86.1\n    23→\n    24→- Added a reasoning_effort setting for GPT-5 models and disabled temperature by default for the GPT-5 family.\n    25→\n    26→### Aider v0.86.0\n    27→\n    28→- Expanded GPT-5 model support across family variants and providers (OpenAI, Azure, OpenRouter), including dated and chat/mini/nano variants.\n    29→- Aider wrote 88% of the code in this release.\n    30→\n    31→### Aider v0.85.5\n    32→\n    33→- Enforced diff edit format for GPT-5 models.\n    34→- Added support for the reasoning_effort setting for GPT-5 models.\n    35→- Fixed model detection to correctly apply GPT-5 settings to versioned names (gpt-5 and gpt-5-2025-08-07).\n    36→\n    37→### Aider v0.85.4\n    38→\n    39→- Added support for openai/gpt-5\n    40→- Fixed analytics to support the latest PostHog SDK event-capture API.\n    41→- Disabled temperature when using GPT-5 models for more deterministic outputs.\n    42→\n    43→### Aider v0.85.3\n    44→\n    45→- Bumped dependencies to pick up latest litellm==1.75.0.\n    46→\n    47→### Aider v0.85.2\n    48→\n    49→- Added support for Grok-4 via `xai/grok-4` and `openrouter/x-ai/grok-4` model names.\n    50→- Added support for `gemini/gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-06-17` model, by Tamir Zahavi-Brunner.\n    51→- `/clear` now prints “All chat history cleared.” so you know it worked, by Zexin Yuan.\n    52→- `/undo` output now shows only the first line of each commit message, making it easier to read.\n    53→- Fixed an issue where new settings for an existing model didn't replace the old ones, by Andrew Grigorev.\n    54→- Added support for `openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2` model, by Jack Harrington.\n    55→\n    56→### Aider v0.85.1\n    57→\n    58→- Display model announcements with no-arg `/model` command.\n    59→\n    60→### Aider v0.85.0\n    61→\n    62→- Support for Responses API models like o1-pro, o3-pro.\n    63→- Updated pricing for o3.\n    64→- Added support for new Gemini models including `gemini-2.5-pro`, `gemini-2.5-flash`, and `gemini-2.5-pro-preview-06-05` with thinking tokens support.\n    65→- Updated model aliases: `flash` now points to `gemini-2.5-flash` and `gemini` now points to `gemini-2.5-pro`.\n    66→- Added `--add-gitignore-files` flag to enable adding files listed in .gitignore to Aider's editing scope, by omarcinkonis.\n    67→- Added `--commit-language` option to specify the language for commit messages, by Kyosuke Takayama.\n    68→- Enhanced thinking tokens support: can now be disabled by setting to 0, and improved help text with examples.\n    69→- Added MATLAB language support for repository maps, by Matthew Tofano.\n    70→- Added support for OpenAI o3-pro model across multiple providers.\n    71→- Improved GitHub Copilot token handling with better validation and error messages, by Vincent Taverna and Sebastian Estrella.\n    72→- Fixed encoding issues in git diff output and LLM history logging.\n    73→- Enhanced commit message generation to use system prompt prefixes, by Luke Reeves.\n    74→- Improved inline code rendering in Rich markdown output, by Vamsi Talupula.\n    75→- Fixed Vertex AI model name prefixes in settings, by Wietse Venema.\n    76→- Improved `/read-only` command to resolve literal paths correctly, by Matteo Landi.\n    77→- Skip expensive file tracking operations when `--skip-sanity-check-repo` is enabled for better performance, by Makar Ivashko.\n    78→- Ensure pip is available before package installation.\n    79→- Auto-create parent directories for chat history files to prevent startup errors, by contributor.\n    80→- Fixed search block regex to accept optional closing tags when working with HTML content, by Mathis Beer.\n    81→- Co-authored-by attribution is now enabled by default for commit messages.\n    82→- Added Clojure language support for repository maps, by Garrett Hopper.\n    83→- Added custom PostHog analytics configuration options with `--analytics-posthog-host` and `--analytics-posthog-project-api-key` flags, by Vasil Markoukin.\n    84→- Optimized chat history summarization performance, by jayeshthk.\n    85→- Improved kebab-case identifier recognition in repository maps for better code analysis.\n    86→- Increased max tokens for Deepseek models to 65536 for better performance.\n    87→- Aider wrote 21% of the code in this release.\n    88→\n    89→### Aider v0.84.0\n    90→\n    91→- Added support for new Claude models including the Sonnet 4 and Opus 4 series (e.g., `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`,\n    92→`claude-opus-4-20250514`) across various providers. The default `sonnet` and `opus` aliases were updated to these newer\n    93→versions.\n    94→- Added support for the `vertex_ai/gemini-2.5-flash-preview-05-20` model.\n    95→- Fixed OpenRouter token cost calculation for improved accuracy.\n    96→- Updated default OpenRouter models during onboarding to `deepseek/deepseek-r1:free` for the free tier and\n    97→`anthropic/claude-sonnet-4` for paid tiers.\n    98→- Automatically refresh GitHub Copilot tokens when used as OpenAI API keys, by Lih Chen.\n    99→- Aider wrote 79% of the code in this release.\n   100→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
