Add `--workspace <path>` to provide a working directory context\n    53→- Add `--raw` to view the full model response (useful for debugging prompt outputs)\n    54→\n    55→### 4. Generate HTML Report\n    56→```bash\n    57→yarn start [date]\n    58→```\n    59→- Generates HTML report from workspace markdown files\n    60→- Date defaults to today if not specified (YYYY-MM-DD format)\n    61→- Combines all markdown files and processes them with Claude Agent SDK\n    62→- Outputs to `run.log` in the workspace directory\n    63→\n    64→## Project Structure\n    65→\n    66→```\n    67→agentdaily/\n    68→├── src/\n    69→│   ├── cli.ts              # CLI entry point with argument parsing\n    70→│   ├── agent/\n    71→│   │   ├── ClaudeAgent.ts  # Claude Agent SDK wrapper\n    72→│   │   └── prompts.ts      # Agent prompts configuration\n    73→│   ├── config/\n    74→│   │   └── tasks.ts        # Research tasks configuration\n    75→│   ├── types/\n    76→│   │   └── index.ts        # TypeScript type definitions\n    77→│   ├── utils/\n    78→│   │   ├── workspace.ts    # Workspace directory management\n    79→│   │   └── formatter.ts    # Output formatting utilities\n    80→│   └── workflows/\n    81→│       ├── update.ts       # Main update workflow with Claude Agent SDK\n    82→│       ├── list.ts         # List-only workflow (read-only mode)\n    83→│       └── research.ts     # Core research workflow orchestration\n    84→├── dist/                   # Compiled JavaScript output\n    85→├── updates/                # Generated daily reports (YYYY-MM-DD/)\n    86→├── prompts/                # Prompt templates for various tasks\n    87→├── package.json            # Project configuration\n    88→└── tsconfig.json           # TypeScript configuration\n    89→\n    90→```\n    91→\n    92→## Development\n    93→\n    94→### Prerequisites\n    95→- Node.js >= 18.0.0\n    96→- Yarn package manager\n    97→\n    98→### Setup\n    99→```bash\n   100→# Install dependencies\n   101→yarn install\n   102→\n   103→# Build TypeScript\n   104→yarn build\n   105→\n   106→# Watch mode for development\n   107→yarn dev\n   108→\n   109→# Clean build artifacts\n   110→yarn clean\n   111→```\n   112→\n   113→### TypeScript Configuration\n   114→- Target: ES2022\n   115→- Module: CommonJS\n   116→- Strict mode enabled\n   117→- Source maps and declarations generated\n   118→\n   119→## Usage Examples\n   120→\n   121→Example index page (static): https://crazygo.github.io/agentdaily/updates/index.html\n   122→\n   123→Last updated: 2025-11-26T16:46:02.361Z\n   124→\n   125→**Daily automated report:**\n   126→```bash\n   127→# Generates report in updates/2025-11-20/\n   128→yarn update\n   129→```\n   130→\n   131→**Custom workspace for testing:**\n   132→```bash\n   133→# Use a specific directory\n   134→yarn update -- --workspace /tmp/test-workspace\n   135→```\n   136→\n   137→**Preview mode:**\n   138→```bash\n   139→# See what would be generated without writing files\n   140→yarn update -- --list\n   141→```\n   142→\n   143→**Generate HTML report:**\n   144→```bash\n   145→# Generate report for today\n   146→yarn start\n   147→\n   148→# Generate report for specific date\n   149→yarn start 2025-11-20\n   150→```\n   151→\n   152→## Architecture\n   153→\n   154→### Yarn Workspace Setup\n   155→This project uses Yarn with workspace support for potential monorepo expansion. The current structure allows for adding packages under `packages/*` in the future.\n   156→\n   157→### Workflow Design\n   158→- **Update Workflow**: Integrates with Claude Agent SDK to autonomously research products, track updates, and compile insights\n   159→- **List Workflow**: Provides read-only preview functionality for CI/CD validation or dry-runs\n   160→- **Research Workflow**: Core orchestration layer that executes configured tasks and aggregates results\n   161→- **Workspace Management**: Automatic date-based organization with fallback to custom paths\n   162→- **HTML Generation**: Processes markdown reports into formatted HTML output using Claude Agent SDK\n   163→\n   164→## Roadmap\n   165→\n   166→- [x] Integrate Claude Agent SDK for autonomous research\n   167→- [x] Add configurable task system for research workflows\n   168→- [ ] Add whitelist product configuration\n   169→- [ ] Implement leader opinion tracking from Twitter/X, blogs, and forums\n   170→- [ ] Add email/Slack notifications for daily reports\n   171→- [ ] Create web interface for browsing historical reports\n   172→- [ ] Add RSS feed generation\n   173→- [ ] Enhance HTML report formatting and styling\n   174→\n   175→## License\n   176→\n   177→MIT\n   178→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
